                  />

                  <FeaturedTestimonial />
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="library-docs">
                <div>
                  <h3>Use the right pattern</h3>

                  <ul>
                    <li>Testimonials: multiple short approved reviews from real clients or customers.</li>
                    <li>FeaturedTestimonial: one strong, detailed review or a key client story.</li>
                    <li>ProjectHighlight: use when proof is better expressed as a project or case study than as a quote.</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>

                <aside class="library-note library-note--warning">
                  <strong>Never invent reviews:</strong> review quotes, names,
                  attribution, star scores, business logos, and performance claims must
                  be genuine and approved for publication.
                </aside>
              </div>
            </section>

            <section id="faqs" class="library-section">
              <div class="library-section-heading">
                <div>
                  <p class="library-section-number">25 — FAQs</p>
                  <h2>Remove the questions that block conversion</h2>
                </div>

                <p class="library-component-file">
                  File: <code>src/components/sections/FAQ.astro</code>
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="library-preview">
                <FAQ />
              </div>

              <div class="library-docs">
                <div>
                  <h3>FAQ topics that matter</h3>

                  <ul>
                    <li>How a client requests service or books.</li>
                    <li>What happens after first contact.</li>
                    <li>Where the business serves.</li>
                    <li>How estimates, pricing, or consultation fees work.</li>
                    <li>What visitors should prepare or bring.</li>
                    <li>Accurate policies, timing, availability, or cancellation terms.</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>

                <aside class="library-note">
                  <strong>Keep it useful:</strong> do not write FAQ entries only for
                  keyword repetition. Answer the real objections and questions staff
                  hear from potential customers.
                </aside>
              </div>
            </section>

            <section id="ctas" class="library-section">
              <div class="library-section-heading">
                <div>
                  <p class="library-section-number">26 — Calls to action</p>
                  <h2>End pages with an appropriate next action</h2>
                </div>

                <p class="library-component-file">
                  Files: <code>ContactCTA.astro</code>, <code>EmergencyCTA.astro</code>, and <code>MobileCTA.astro</code>
                </p>
