              <div class="library-preview">
                <div class="library-variant-stack">
                  <ContactCTA
                    title="High-contrast final CTA"
                    description="Use after a visitor has learned about services, proof, process, and next steps."
                  />

                  <EmergencyCTA />
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="library-docs">
                <div>
                  <h3>CTA selection guide</h3>

                  <ul>
                    <li>ContactCTA: estimate requests, general inquiries, consultations, and standard lead generation.</li>
                    <li>EmergencyCTA: only when a client genuinely offers urgent/emergency response.</li>
                    <li>PhoneCTA: high-intent service and local-business pages.</li>
                    <li>ServiceAreaCTA: reinforce geographic relevance when visitors need to verify coverage.</li>
                    <li>MobileCTA: smaller-screen conversion support for phone-first sites.</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>

                <aside class="library-note library-note--warning">
                  <strong>Be accurate:</strong> only use wording such as “emergency,”
                  “same-day,” “free estimate,” “book now,” or “available today” if the
                  client confirms they can consistently meet that promise.
                </aside>
              </div>
            </section>

